## Review usage

- Provider counters are reported as `measured`, `estimated` or `unavailable`: a counter the
  provider did not expose is `unavailable`, never a guessed number; an estimate is labelled.
- The normal-candidate target is at most 35 assistant turns. It is a turn target, not a token
  ceiling, and no numeric token budget is enforced or claimed before a measured pilot.
- An unfinished review is an `incomplete-review`: it keeps the candidate evidence and never
  integrates a truncated diff.

## Provenance

This report records an autonomous review decision bound to the commits, tree
and check results above. Any change to the staged candidate requires a fresh
review and a newly rendered report. No manual sign-off is required.

